    "media:imagetext": "BOEING 707-320C\nIf an emergency should arise\nthe crew of this aircraft have been trained to cope\nwith such an unlikely event. If such a landing is\nnecessary you will be adequately forewarned.\nKeep calm and obey instructions.\nChange in cabin pressure\nCabin pressure is controlled at a level best suited\nto your comfort. Should a sudden change in\npressure occur, extinquish cigarettes. Individual\noxygen masks will be lowered automatically in\nfront of your face. This mask should be pulled\ndown and placed over the mouth and nose to\nensure comfortable breathing.\nBRACING\nEscape Slide\nIn the event of an evacuation (on land)\nAdjust seats to a full upright position.\nLoosen neckwear, remove glasses, false teeth,\nhigh heeled shoes and all sharp objects such as\npencils, badges, etc.\nFasten seat belt around hips.\nWhen instructed to brace take up the following\nposition: Place feet apart on floor, fold arms on\nknees and lean forward.\nRemain in this position until further instructions\nare given by the crew.\nThe crew will open exits.\nAll exits are clearly marked.\nEMERGENCY EXITS\nCARGO\nPASSENGER\nVERSION\nMIXED\nPASSENGER\nVERSION\nn 7900906\nBOEING 707-320",
