    "millsfield:images_texts": [
      "Wenn Sie den Inhalt dieses Merkblattes nicht verstehen\nkönnen, erkundigen Sie sich, bitte, bie der Stewardess.\nSi vous ne comprenez pas cette brochure veuillez vous\ninformer auprès de l'hôtesse.\nIn the event of ditching (on water)\nIf such a landing is necessary you will receive prior warning. Keep calm and obey\ninstructions. Adjust seats to full upright position. Remove sharp objects, spectacles,\ndentures and high-heeled shoes. Loosen collar and necktie. Keep all other clothing\non. Put on life-jacket. DO NOT INFLATE INSIDE AIRCRAFT.\nFASTEN SEAT BELT AROUND HIPS. Remain seated. When instructed to brace\ntake up the following position:\nPlace feet apart on floor, fold arms on knees and lean forward. Remain in this position\nuntil further instructions are given by the crew. All exits are clearly marked. The crew\nwill open exits, launch and inflate liferafts. A calm, purposeful approach will do much\nto avert panic when leaving the aircraft.\nAll persons boarding the Liferafts, should sit on the high side, backs against the\ntubes, feet towards the centre and hold on to the lifeline which encircles the raft.\nA crew member is assigned to each raft. The rafts are equipped to keep you com-\nfortable until help arrives. Each raft has a radio and distress signals.\nYour hostess will demonstrate this life vest procedure.\n1 Slip the life vest over\nyour head with the narrow\nstraps at the back.\n2 The long straps at the back 3 Pull tabs until straps 4. Do not inflate your life\nshould be brought forward\nare tight around your\nvest inside the aircraft.\nTo\nwaist.\ninflate pull knobs\nand hooked to the metal rings.\nstraiaht down.\nMay also be inflated by\nblowing in both rubber\ntubes.\nBaby survival cots are available,\nthe hostess\nwill\nexplain\ntheir\nuse.\nDO NOT USE A CIGARETTE LIGHTER WHICH HAS A TRANSPARENT FUEL CONTAINER\n2011-04\nPLEASE DO NOT TAKE THIS CARD FROM THE AIRCRAFT"
    ],
